00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Hmm.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.000
Whitney Hodges: Good. Good to hear. Awesome.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.000
Bri Garofalo: Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:29.000
Bri Garofalo: I just wanted to check in on the senior ad. How is that going? I know you sent me all of that, like, stuff, but I can never really understand it unless someone's telling me.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmhm.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, do you want to kind of break it down, Carmen?

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, no worries.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:47.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yes. Everything on the family side is good. I know you asked about the senior photos one. It has very low search volume. Everything I put in for keywords is about 10 searches a month on average in that 30A area.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.000
Bri Garofalo: Okay.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.000
Bri Garofalo: Mm-hmm.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:04:02.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Uh, so it is harder for us to get traction with getting impressions, getting clicks. I did broaden it to be anything senior-like, which I know is not ideal, uh, but we're still only getting impressions and not clicks, so I'm not sure… is it the season for people to be searching for seniors?

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Senior photo things right now.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.000
Bri Garofalo: Hmm, maybe not. I've no…

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.000
Whitney Hodges: That's…

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:14.000
Bri Garofalo: Well, I mean, I get senior inquiries, for sure, but…

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:19.000
Bri Garofalo: They're not, like, high volume or anything, but maybe it's not the right season.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:24.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Maybe not. When do you notice the most, like, inquiries for that service?

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:36.000
Bri Garofalo: You know what, it's always… it's pretty stable, where it's, like, just not very often in general. Probably, like, I would say, like, less than 10 a month.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.000
Whitney Hodges: Yep.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.000
Bri Garofalo: Reach out about senior photos.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmm.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:57.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm. I think… I don't know if you do meta, I feel like if that was on Instagram, that would be really hot with seniors, you know, like, they would really love to see that, especially the visual, and they're like, oh, I didn't even know I needed that. Uh… that's just a thought, but… yeah, I think it's… I don't think it's hurting you, though, having it run, because maybe one.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.000
Bri Garofalo: Yeah.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:01.000
Carmen Cruickshank: all these people searching for it, and then you're spending it well, if that makes sense.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:05.000
Bri Garofalo: That's true, because I don't pay for it unless they click, right?

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.000
Carmen Cruickshank: uh…

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah, thank you.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Exactly. Yeah.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:20.000
Bri Garofalo: So then it doesn't hurt at this point to let it run, and then, like you said, there might be a spike that… I mean, I don't know how the trends are exactly, so maybe, you know, the spike happens while it's running, and then it ends up being good.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:32.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Exactly. Like, it might be beginning of August when school starts, or September, and then it's running well. I think the only issue keeping a campaign on is if it's getting clicks and then not getting leads, because then it's just a waste of money. So, yeah.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:36.000
Bri Garofalo: Right, but at this point, it's not getting clicks, right?

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:44.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm, exactly. Yeah, so if we see, again, there's that spike of clicks and interaction with the site, but no leads, then it's like, okay, let's reconsider what's.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.000
Bri Garofalo: Okay, cool.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Okay.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.000
Whitney Hodges: Mmhm.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:51.000
Bri Garofalo: Yeah. I feel like maybe maybe, you know, like, in August.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:56.000
Bri Garofalo: It'll spike, but I guess it's one of those things you just have to test.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mmhm.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Exactly. Or you'll never know.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.000
Bri Garofalo: Yeah.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:16.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah. Yeah. So there may be more kind of traction with back to school. That would be my guess. But we'll be able to kind of see, I think, you know, kind of when the time comes. But, you know, we've been seeing that for some time now, just the family portraits have been.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:22.000
Whitney Hodges: doing really well, and I think that campaign looks pretty stable, right, from what you've been seeing, Carmen?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm, definitely.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:41.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, okay, awesome. So, I know we had talked, um, Bree, about us kind of, you know, at some point over the summer, kind of transitioning out of the full-service ads management, and it moving more to, like, you know, to where you're kind of responsible for it, but we can be available on a more.

